# trailing_zeros:
# CSES 1618, Trailing Zeros (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1618), in our own
# words: the number n! of orderings of n different things ends in some number of
# zeros when written in decimal; the number of those zeros. The input is a binary
# natural (corpora/library/binary/natural) n >= 1, and the answer a binary
# natural. Part of the CSES port's third batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: n! is computed as the product 1 * 2 *
# ... * n, and then divided by ten, its decimal digits found from the low end of the
# binary numeral (ten_quotient_remainder, as `removing_digits` does), for as long as the remainder is zero,
# counting the divisions. Its reading takes about n multiplications of numbers of
# about n log n bits, then one division by ten per zero; the replacement the family asks
# for is Legendre's formula, the zeros of n! being the sum of n / 5^k over k >= 1, about
# log n steps on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal (the ten is
# written with binary_zero, binary_even and binary_odd). It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since the
# product consumes the bounded gap n - k, ten_quotient_remainder consumes a binary numeral,
# and the counting of the zeros consumes a positive number (n! >= 1) that its quotient
# by ten, taken only when the remainder is zero, makes smaller, so that it reaches a number with a
# nonzero last digit, as every positive number does after finitely many zeros; the
# branches that a Scott boolean discards are never read. binary_subtract, which writes no top
# (../common/binary_modular), is asked only to subtract ten from a remainder that is
# not below ten. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable
# equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ _ false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ merge_binary_times _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ binary_double binary_subtract _ _
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd binary_zero))
λ ten
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ quotient remainder continue
    . binary_less_than remainder ten (continue (binary_double quotient) remainder) (continue (binary_odd quotient) (binary_subtract remainder ten false))
  )
λ settle
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self natural
    . natural (λcontinue. continue binary_zero binary_zero)
      (λhalf continue. self half λquotient remainder. settle quotient (binary_double remainder) continue)
      λhalf continue. self half λquotient remainder. settle quotient (binary_odd remainder) continue
  )
λ ten_quotient_remainder
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ limit
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self factor product
        . binary_less_than limit factor product (self (merge_binary_increment factor) (merge_binary_times product factor))
      ) one one
  )
λ factorial
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self number count
    . ten_quotient_remainder number
      λ quotient remainder
      . remainder (self quotient (merge_binary_increment count)) (λ_. count) λ_. count
  )
λ zeros_of
. (λtuple. tuple λlimit. zeros_of (factorial limit) binary_zero)
λ trailing_zeros
. export trailing_zeros
